{"title":"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">2015 AMC 12A #19</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">2015 AMC 10A #24</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Less_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Less Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, there is a quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with positive integer side lengths, perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, right angles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5204a6910d20a4ff2968ad55671e3cfa350e9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78370380065fe52b79c06578e860784b1072d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=AD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.  How many different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9a348230e436bef36aa463b1693b22a4c8fbf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt;2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> are possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c08b66d5dae02b8c44f50b3177c462534595dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }30\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }31\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }61\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }62\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b13a806ee59da256367d4cbdb66f73a22533c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a821b6b87614973eebedefdbab9a3057b45466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = AD = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> be positive integers. Drop a perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> to show that, using the Pythagorean Theorem, that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd48499079a7d0fe961c38c747cdb79950c68aab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + (y - 2)^2 = y^2.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />\nSimplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/64153a14f214b7b2ccc95c030683069bf8b78340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 4y + 4 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f654d4d00f4f15f5eaeca9c10bfa1378f22698a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 4(y - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is one more than a perfect square.\n</p><p>The perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba967e06e62c08f9ca58d44b58f8fbd368926ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2 + x + 2y = 2y + 2\\sqrt{y - 1} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"22\" /> must be less than 2015. Simple calculations demonstrate that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3d82f13287873823a3e01fc78afde9c5fbbead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 31^2 + 1 = 962$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> is valid, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751826d3ba7684437fb26037df8cc90dc0ea3098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 32^2 + 1 = 1025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> is not. On the lower side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234b330118777aba0bee513e3ade547ebd70d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> does not work (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />), but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe5c19851676c19d5816abb31ffa026ecabaadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> does work. Hence, there are 31 valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e420e03f7063ba341ae26a10e9a8adf93aaf5e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = n^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6937765be6dcbe31edb393a55c7c9402b3a74bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le n \\le 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />), and so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fdc44582dca596a79d36af6f8ac936f1cbb6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b13a806ee59da256367d4cbdb66f73a22533c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c912c8785e2a6b54337f46e29f78e4d6f0a732f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = AD = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers. Drop a perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Denote the intersection point of the perpendicular and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />'s length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, as well.\nCall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed3662c82b340e930819688a03a8888bb70db30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = (y + 2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />.\nAnd so: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9fff039e5b605468140744695dcd96dde5a6fbdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 4y + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fe721a50808aa26c7bb1b1e75b6117868dc77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (x^2-4)/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Writing this down and testing, it appears that this holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. However, since there is a dividend of 4, the numerator must be divisible by 4 to conform to the criteria that the side lengths are positive integers.\nIn effect, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be a multiple of 2 to let the side lengths be integers. We test, and soon reach 62. It gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f917397ef7734f70bba02f1f3cc5fcca5a607c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 1988$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, which is less than 2015. However, 64 gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c724891a5cffdf5e387763998e8ec5fd8ac5a9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2116 &gt; 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />, so we know 62 is the largest we can go up to. Count all the even numbers from 2 to 62, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fdc44582dca596a79d36af6f8ac936f1cbb6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-jackshi2006\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Less_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Less_Counting)\">Solution 3 (Less Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Less Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/55877befb7fc814ccd29222b50c6e23d1d17401d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f62fe52ff3bbe5a8373430aaa1ed24d504cf11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = AD = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers. Drop a perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Denote the intersection point of the perpendicular and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />'s length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a848b287a40bf4a8737f06fc35ea5b77af32e977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED = m-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b85357c7bdb9a550101eda99c1dcad137fb4fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 = (m-2)^2 + n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />\n, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7c2ba4fffe21f1444c2ede416ba290778e00d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 = 4(m-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Notice that 4 is already a perfect square and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96eec32de93b032b6d531a03aa5b346156b62a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> also has to be a perfect square. \nWe can denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96eec32de93b032b6d531a03aa5b346156b62a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, therefore we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a02b1b7a3fe9a6b1adce61f3fba718d8c1b702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = x^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/17216fab66415b52c8edff82bedc23da7dfc2825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, and each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will correspond to a pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6d6f10a89b538ad0258486aee2c78a801c7f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9a348230e436bef36aa463b1693b22a4c8fbf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt;2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41fce6cfe8dc8e2a259f1cfdf4473a3a6fa66db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + n + m + m&lt;2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"15\" /> which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d8ab4b9ac2ae4503f4c87d60561bdd28e5ae81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2m&lt;2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaacd7d4503267249e0208aea83a700b0dfa3b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+2(x^2 + 1) &lt; 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" />, simplify this will again give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89b4a75e9450fd0e907d978ac3c6677038ff0681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x + 1 &lt; 1006.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\nTry <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5361e7974d96db803e913bba80f779505beb54a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 32$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74ccf6cc9e53841e84193e5a1b51511aee282d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x + 1 = 1057 &gt; 1006.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />, exceeded\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1875c5bfd7db8f3b23b14a97b76e2f4a8c122ef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18a135d633554b668aa05f2a3b76d54a1b7ae695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x + 1 = 993 &lt; 1006.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1875c5bfd7db8f3b23b14a97b76e2f4a8c122ef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> works for us.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0e4940d43e6b6313ba59e160cf570f79483a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871059aab5e228102cdf0df0e359e3184b311b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^2 + x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" /> increases, therefore for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fcfcd740d1f198bb5abfc4fdd52a8196ebc21ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d3a40c128f3b68e28ea3baf72c9178a686a6111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) &lt; f(31) &lt; 1006.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313a167517f0e76ef443a5e209d75855d50845f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, 31]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy the condition that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89b4a75e9450fd0e907d978ac3c6677038ff0681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x + 1 &lt; 1006.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> needs to be integer, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> integers in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313a167517f0e76ef443a5e209d75855d50845f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, 31]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> corresponds to a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6d6f10a89b538ad0258486aee2c78a801c7f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, meaning there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible value for different pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6d6f10a89b538ad0258486aee2c78a801c7f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> and lead to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fdc44582dca596a79d36af6f8ac936f1cbb6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> possible values for the perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Andy_li0805\">Andy_li0805</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2015amc10a/398\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2015amc10a/398</a>\n</p><p>~ RANGANATH12\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9DSv4zn7MyE\">https://youtu.be/9DSv4zn7MyE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A\">2015 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\